WEBVTT

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:08.420
"AUGUST 6, 2095
SPEED SHOOTING ROOKIE EVENT
QUALIFYING ROUNDS"

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:10.960
"AUGUST 6, 2095
SPEED SHOOTING ROOKIE EVENT
QUALIFYING ROUNDS"

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:10.960
This is Day Four of the Nine Schools Competition.

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:13.010
"AUGUST 6, 2095
SPEED SHOOTING ROOKIE EVENT
QUALIFYING ROUNDS"

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:13.010
Today marks the start of the Rookie Events...

00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:16.550
and the qualifying rounds for Speed Shooting
are being held right now.

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:33.530
Wh-What's going on here?

00:00:33.530 --> 00:00:35.910
Does she have air mines set up or something?

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:38.490
I've never seen magic like this before!

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:44.120
Shiori, do you know
what kind of tactics she used?

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:45.330
Yes.

00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:49.380
Ms. Kitayama must've divided
the field into multiple sections

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:53.720
and activated Oscillation Magic
at the areas where the clay scattered.

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:56.720
I wonder what would happen
if she competed against you.

00:00:56.720 --> 00:00:59.390
Let's see. The use of these tactics tells me

00:00:59.390 --> 00:01:02.850
that Ms. Kitayama has a problem
with range specification.

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:04.600
After the semifinals,

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:07.560
the format will change to one
where two types of clay will scatter.

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:11.940
That will call for magic
of even higher precision.

00:01:14.110 --> 00:01:15.490
Perfect.

00:01:15.490 --> 00:01:17.160
"SHIZUKU KITAYAMA (FIRST HIGH SCHOOL)"

00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:20.200
That's my specialty.

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:25.120
If I make full use of my calculation prowess,
I can nullify her magic.

00:01:33.510 --> 00:01:36.050
You're Ms. Kitayama
of First High, aren't you?

00:01:36.050 --> 00:01:40.510
Hello. I'm Shiori Kanou of Third High.

00:01:40.510 --> 00:01:42.220
Nice to meet you.

00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:44.930
I can see that you're extremely skilled.

00:01:44.930 --> 00:01:48.440
I can't wait to take you on
in the semifinals.

00:01:48.440 --> 00:01:49.560
I see.

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:53.980
Meaning you don't intend
for a second to lose before that.

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:58.070
Fine. I'll be looking forward
to the semifinals, too.

00:02:07.210 --> 00:02:10.380
Watch me, Airi.

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:13.380
I won't let you down, no matter what.

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:52.020
"SHIORI KANOU (THIRD HIGH SCHOOL)"
"ROOKIE EVENT"
"QUALIFYING ROUND FIRST ATTEMPT"

00:03:59.190 --> 00:04:03.410
Secondary clear. Tertiary correct.

00:04:03.410 --> 00:04:04.660
What's that?

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:07.950
If she's using Oscillation Magic
to destroy the first clay target,

00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:11.370
then how can those fragments hit
the other targets one after the other?

00:04:11.370 --> 00:04:12.960
A Movement Spell, maybe?

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:14.870
You mean she knows
where all those fragments are,

00:04:14.870 --> 00:04:17.420
and she's sending each one
in different directions?

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:20.760
But just grasping the location
of the object you're moving is hard enough.

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:24.220
How can she handle each fragment's
movement in an instant?

00:04:24.220 --> 00:04:27.220
Only a supercomputer could do that!

00:04:27.220 --> 00:04:30.180
Don't tell me that's exactly what she's doing!

00:04:30.180 --> 00:04:32.640
It looks like her precision
is even sharper now.

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:33.020
"2092 (3 YEARS AGO)"

00:04:33.020 --> 00:04:36.520
"2092 (3 YEARS AGO)"

00:04:33.020 --> 00:04:36.520
I knew I wasn't wrong about her.

00:04:46.530 --> 00:04:51.240
You can reach even greater heights.

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:55.170
Don't you want to see
the same scenery as me?

00:04:55.170 --> 00:04:58.590
Shiori honed her natural spatial recognition
and calculation skills

00:04:58.590 --> 00:05:03.260
at the Kanazawa Magical Physics Institute.

00:05:03.260 --> 00:05:04.800
As a result...

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:08.680
she acquired special eyesight that allows her
to instantly convert anything she sees

00:05:08.680 --> 00:05:10.560
into numerical formulas
applicable to magic.

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:13.350
Shiori is able to predict everything.

00:05:13.350 --> 00:05:15.100
The trajectory of all particles,

00:05:15.100 --> 00:05:17.650
which appears random to most eyes.

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:21.110
Magic that belongs to Shiori alone,
which can't be mimicked.

00:05:21.110 --> 00:05:25.820
The gorgeous melody of formulas
produced by calculating ability

00:05:25.820 --> 00:05:28.570
superior to any supercomputer!

00:05:28.570 --> 00:05:30.780
Arithmetic Chain!

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:32.660
"SHIORI KANOU (THIRD HIGH SCHOOL)"

00:05:36.160 --> 00:05:40.540
I've analyzed the magic
Ms. Kitayama used in the quarterfinals.

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:43.090
To make her clay targets easier to hit,

00:05:43.090 --> 00:05:48.220
she cast Convergence Magic
to increase their density relative to space.

00:05:50.180 --> 00:05:51.430
Like that.

00:05:51.430 --> 00:05:56.810
This changed the trajectory of her
opponent's clay, resulting in a low score.

00:05:56.810 --> 00:05:58.100
As you know,

00:05:58.100 --> 00:06:04.030
the specialized CAD that she's using
can store up to nine activation sequences.

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:09.740
Since Ms. Kitayama was using them separately,
it fooled her opponent, as well.

00:06:09.740 --> 00:06:15.120
But you'd be able to handle all nine
of those sequences, wouldn't you?

00:06:19.580 --> 00:06:21.040
"SHIZUKU KITAYAMA (FIRST HIGH SCHOOL)"
"SHIORI KANOU (THIRD HIGH SCHOOL)"

00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:35.430
Her opponent's clay
is being thrown off course!

00:06:35.430 --> 00:06:37.850
That's Shizuku's win-at-all-costs strategy!

00:06:37.850 --> 00:06:39.850
No, that's not what that is.

00:06:39.850 --> 00:06:40.940
That's...

00:06:43.770 --> 00:06:46.280
Even if they're off course,
the chain's still unbroken?

00:06:46.280 --> 00:06:49.900
Does that mean she's reversed
Shizuku's magic?

00:06:49.900 --> 00:06:51.570
Not that Shizuku's not amazing, as well,

00:06:51.570 --> 00:06:54.370
but Ms. Kanou is racking up points
at an even faster clip!

00:06:54.370 --> 00:06:55.830
No way!

00:06:55.830 --> 00:06:57.450
Shizuku Kitayama...

00:06:57.450 --> 00:07:01.880
Your mother is a magician renowned around
the world, and your father is a man of means.

00:07:01.880 --> 00:07:05.960
Your magical talents are being nurtured
thanks to such a support system.

00:07:05.960 --> 00:07:09.380
It's the complete opposite
of my own plight.

00:07:09.380 --> 00:07:12.140
My family lost its number
and fell into ruin.

00:07:12.140 --> 00:07:14.470
My parents fought nonstop.

00:07:14.470 --> 00:07:18.520
Back then, I just wanted
to abandon everything I had.

00:07:22.770 --> 00:07:26.900
It was that hand
that guided me into the light.

00:07:28.360 --> 00:07:31.450
The moment I took her hand,
I made up my mind

00:07:31.450 --> 00:07:34.820
that I'd never go back to that place again!

00:07:34.820 --> 00:07:38.290
My only goal is to advance
toward victory by Airi's side!

00:07:40.250 --> 00:07:42.710
This isn't looking too good, right?

00:07:42.710 --> 00:07:44.130
Right.

00:07:44.130 --> 00:07:45.880
Shizuku...

00:07:45.880 --> 00:07:48.000
Don't worry, Honoka.

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:51.380
Who's Shizuku's engineer, after all?

00:07:52.720 --> 00:07:56.390
There's no way that my brother
doesn't have a countermeasure in place.

00:08:00.180 --> 00:08:01.730
Something's wrong.

00:08:01.730 --> 00:08:04.190
I'm more exhausted
than I thought I'd be.

00:08:04.190 --> 00:08:08.150
No matter how draining
Arithmetic Chain can be as a spell,

00:08:08.150 --> 00:08:13.910
simulating Ms. Kitayama's tactics
should keep it optimally adjusted.

00:08:13.910 --> 00:08:15.740
So, why...

00:08:16.870 --> 00:08:18.080
Don't tell me...

00:08:21.120 --> 00:08:22.750
This isn't good, is it, Joji?

00:08:22.750 --> 00:08:23.920
Right.

00:08:23.920 --> 00:08:26.290
Ms. Kitayama's CAD...

00:08:26.290 --> 00:08:27.750
Most likely, it's...

00:08:27.750 --> 00:08:29.250
a generalized device!

00:08:29.250 --> 00:08:33.510
Just as I thought, they were sure
it was specialized and strategized accordingly.

00:08:33.510 --> 00:08:34.800
Unfortunately for you,

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:39.560
that's a generalized CAD fitted with auxiliary
sights, which was just unveiled in Germany.

00:08:39.560 --> 00:08:42.430
The number of activation sequences
it can store is 99.

00:08:42.430 --> 00:08:47.190
Unless you have
a countermeasure for all 99...

00:08:47.190 --> 00:08:49.360
I win!

00:08:50.650 --> 00:08:51.740
I missed?

00:08:51.740 --> 00:08:53.240
I didn't see that coming!

00:08:53.240 --> 00:08:57.070
A specialized device could never store
that amount of activation sequences!

00:08:57.070 --> 00:09:02.830
But there were limits on the output levels
for the spells cast in the quarterfinals.

00:09:02.830 --> 00:09:05.750
So, she was deliberately competing
with fewer activation sequences?

00:09:05.750 --> 00:09:07.130
Yes.

00:09:07.130 --> 00:09:10.170
It was probably a tactic to throw us off.

00:09:10.170 --> 00:09:15.470
To make us believe it was a specialized device,
so we'd only counter nine activation sequences!

00:09:15.470 --> 00:09:20.560
But the actual number of activation sequences
is 99. It's a complete overwork.

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:26.100
So, someone came up with this strategy
and crafted a cutting-edge generalized CAD?

00:09:26.100 --> 00:09:30.730
And the player would have to have mad magical
skills to achieve the needed activation speed

00:09:30.730 --> 00:09:34.110
to make us mistake her device
for a specialized CAD.

00:09:34.110 --> 00:09:37.860
A unique strategy maximizing
the player's characteristics.

00:09:37.860 --> 00:09:41.870
Has First High been hiding
an engineer as talented as that?

00:09:41.870 --> 00:09:44.080
Kanou may not know it,

00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:48.330
but it's like she's being forced to run
back and forth across a tennis court.

00:09:48.330 --> 00:09:50.750
She can't last much longer now.

00:09:55.220 --> 00:09:58.970
I can't allow myself
to stop in my tracks here!

00:09:58.970 --> 00:10:00.680
I...

00:10:00.680 --> 00:10:02.140
No...

00:10:02.140 --> 00:10:04.560
I'm never going back there again!

00:10:06.020 --> 00:10:08.270
I don't want to go back!

00:10:08.270 --> 00:10:10.230
I'm joining Airi!

00:10:14.900 --> 00:10:15.780
Winner...

00:10:15.780 --> 00:10:19.860
First High's Shizuku Kitayama!

00:10:19.860 --> 00:10:22.740
She's through to the final!

00:10:27.750 --> 00:10:30.000
These are the final results

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:33.290
of the Women's Speed Shooting Rookie Event.

00:10:33.290 --> 00:10:33.800
"IN USE"

00:10:33.290 --> 00:10:33.800
"THIRD HIGH"

00:10:33.800 --> 00:10:36.760
"IN USE"
"THIRD HIGH"

00:10:33.800 --> 00:10:36.760
First High's piling on their scores
more than we expected.

00:10:36.760 --> 00:10:41.220
None of us saw them sweeping
the Women's Speed Shooting Events.

00:10:41.220 --> 00:10:46.520
The real blow was having Kanou finish fourth
when she was a lock to win!

00:10:46.520 --> 00:10:49.520
Shiori, your opponent
in the battle for third place

00:10:49.520 --> 00:10:52.980
was someone you'd normally beat in your sleep.

00:10:52.980 --> 00:10:56.740
So how could you make one improbable
mistake after another like that?

00:10:56.740 --> 00:11:00.070
Talent-wise, Kanou and Ms. Kitayama
were on the same level.

00:11:00.070 --> 00:11:04.530
Watching that match, Masaki and I
came to a certain conclusion.

00:11:04.530 --> 00:11:05.790
Yeah.

00:11:05.790 --> 00:11:08.410
First High's win was no fluke.

00:11:08.410 --> 00:11:11.580
They've got a beast of an engineer...

00:11:11.580 --> 00:11:14.750
who can raise the level of a CAD's functions
by two or three generations.

00:11:21.970 --> 00:11:23.350
"FIRST HIGH SCHOOL"

00:11:23.350 --> 00:11:25.060
"FIRST HIGH SCHOOL"

00:11:23.350 --> 00:11:25.060
How amazing is this?

00:11:25.060 --> 00:11:26.850
I mean, what a feat...

00:11:26.850 --> 00:11:30.060
for First High to sweep the podium like that!

00:11:30.060 --> 00:11:32.650
It was because of everyone's great efforts.

00:11:32.650 --> 00:11:37.480
That may be part of it, but everyone knows
that your talents played a big role.

00:11:37.480 --> 00:11:41.530
Right! I never dreamed I'd come this far!

00:11:41.530 --> 00:11:43.570
We really appreciate you, Tatsuya!

00:11:43.570 --> 00:11:46.080
My spell, Active Air Mine,

00:11:46.080 --> 00:11:48.950
would've never seen the light of day
if it hadn't been for you, Tatsuya.

00:11:48.950 --> 00:11:50.370
Thank you.

00:11:50.370 --> 00:11:54.040
I only did what I was supposed
to do as your engineer.

00:11:54.040 --> 00:11:56.630
Oh, you're so modest!

00:11:56.630 --> 00:12:02.630
Now that you mention it, they're entering
Active Air Mine into that Magic Index, right?

00:12:02.630 --> 00:12:04.890
As magic that you developed, Tatsuya!

00:12:04.890 --> 00:12:06.970
What? Seriously?

00:12:06.970 --> 00:12:08.100
Yeah.

00:12:08.100 --> 00:12:11.850
Oh boy, your renown
is only going to explode!

00:12:11.850 --> 00:12:15.440
What are we going to do?
He's our secret weapon!

00:12:15.440 --> 00:12:19.860
No. I've registered Active Air Mine
under Kitayama's name.

00:12:19.860 --> 00:12:21.320
What?

00:12:23.200 --> 00:12:25.620
Being overmodest can sound
like sarcasm, you know.

00:12:25.620 --> 00:12:27.580
No, I'm not being modest.

00:12:27.580 --> 00:12:32.290
I just want to be spared the humiliation of not
being able to use the magic I developed myself.

00:12:32.290 --> 00:12:34.580
That's all.

00:12:39.630 --> 00:12:40.880
Shiori!

00:12:40.880 --> 00:12:43.470
I know you're in there. Open up.

00:12:46.430 --> 00:12:49.680
That was my mental weakness.

00:12:49.680 --> 00:12:53.600
It was my weakness
that delivered that defeat

00:12:53.600 --> 00:12:58.360
even though I had to win for Airi's sake!

00:12:58.360 --> 00:13:00.980
I'm finished.

00:13:00.980 --> 00:13:03.030
Don't be so pathetic!

00:13:03.030 --> 00:13:07.530
I acknowledged
the radiance that belongs to you!

00:13:07.530 --> 00:13:11.160
How can you not believe
in that yourself?

00:13:15.540 --> 00:13:19.880
Oh, dear. I doubt that my purification ritual
would work on her in that state.

00:13:19.880 --> 00:13:22.420
I've never seen Shiori like that.

00:13:22.420 --> 00:13:26.300
If she doesn't snap out of it, we might
have to have someone take her place.

00:13:26.300 --> 00:13:28.510
No, it won't come to that.

00:13:28.510 --> 00:13:29.550
What?

00:13:29.550 --> 00:13:32.060
Based on my own gut feeling!

00:13:33.100 --> 00:13:37.520
Right. If that's your gut feeling,
it'll probably turn out that way.

00:13:37.520 --> 00:13:39.270
Yeah!

00:13:39.270 --> 00:13:43.690
And now, the Women's Battle Board
Rookie Event is about to begin!

00:13:48.780 --> 00:13:51.660
It's going to start soon!

00:13:51.660 --> 00:13:55.830
I was focused on Shizuku's match this morning,
so it wasn't on my mind at all,

00:13:55.830 --> 00:13:58.920
but now I'm getting nervous
all of a sudden!

00:14:01.800 --> 00:14:03.210
You.

00:14:05.090 --> 00:14:06.880
Wh-Who are you?

00:14:06.880 --> 00:14:09.510
What are you so nervous about?

00:14:09.510 --> 00:14:11.680
This girl...
I think she's from Third High!

00:14:11.680 --> 00:14:14.890
Is she a spy?
Don't tell me this is obstruction!

00:14:14.890 --> 00:14:19.850
Come to think of it, we still don't know
what caused Ms. Watanabe's accident!

00:14:19.850 --> 00:14:24.070
You have nothing to worry about.
There won't be any accidents.

00:14:24.070 --> 00:14:26.440
Did I say that out loud?

00:14:26.440 --> 00:14:28.110
No need to be nervous.

00:14:28.110 --> 00:14:32.370
As long as you give it your all, you can breeze
right through the qualifying rounds!

00:14:32.370 --> 00:14:34.540
Why would you say that?

00:14:34.540 --> 00:14:38.000
Because I felt like encouraging
another person. That's why.

00:14:38.000 --> 00:14:40.670
--See ya!
--Huh?

00:14:40.670 --> 00:14:42.960
What was that all about?

00:14:42.960 --> 00:14:45.670
But I think I feel
a little more relaxed now.

00:14:45.670 --> 00:14:47.380
Honoka...

00:14:47.380 --> 00:14:48.550
Tatsuya?

00:14:48.550 --> 00:14:50.640
Do you know that girl?

00:14:50.640 --> 00:14:53.430
No, I just spoke with her a bit. That's all.

00:14:53.430 --> 00:14:55.180
She's from Third High, right?

00:14:55.180 --> 00:14:56.520
Right.

00:14:56.520 --> 00:15:00.400
She's the favorite to win
the Battle Board Rookie Event,

00:15:00.400 --> 00:15:03.650
Toko Tsukushiin of Third High School.

00:15:12.780 --> 00:15:15.160
What the...

00:15:15.160 --> 00:15:19.080
I rule the water's surface!
You'd better yield to me!

00:15:19.080 --> 00:15:21.920
I-It's that girl's magic?

00:15:21.920 --> 00:15:26.050
The Tsukushiin Family hails from a long line
of Shinto-type Ancient Magic users,

00:15:26.050 --> 00:15:30.260
and they say that their roots go all the way
back to the great Shinto Clan, the Shirakawas.

00:15:30.260 --> 00:15:31.890
Shirakawa...

00:15:33.050 --> 00:15:38.310
That's right. Just as the name implies,
they're adept at water-related magic.

00:15:41.440 --> 00:15:43.650
So much fun!

00:15:43.650 --> 00:15:45.070
Goal!

00:15:45.070 --> 00:15:49.240
Ms. Tsukushiin just blasted her way through
the qualifying rounds well in first place!

00:15:49.240 --> 00:15:52.910
W-Wow! I've never seen magic like that!

00:15:54.740 --> 00:15:57.830
Don't worry. You have nothing to fear.

00:15:57.830 --> 00:16:02.420
She's a formidable player, but you can
totally hold your own against her, Honoka.

00:16:02.420 --> 00:16:06.420
Just remember all the training
you've undergone until today.

00:16:06.420 --> 00:16:08.210
Tatsuya...

00:16:14.300 --> 00:16:17.310
Everyone's really into it.

00:16:17.310 --> 00:16:23.310
Miyuki seems busy with the Student Council.
Is she finding time to practice?

00:16:23.310 --> 00:16:27.270
So, she's training with Tatsuya.

00:16:27.270 --> 00:16:29.730
I'm leaving it all to you, Brother!

00:16:29.730 --> 00:16:33.490
Well, since I do know
every inch of your body...

00:16:33.490 --> 00:16:36.200
Oh, that feels wonderful!

00:16:36.200 --> 00:16:38.080
No! None of that!

00:16:38.080 --> 00:16:40.500
You're really pouring your heart
into practice, huh?

00:16:40.500 --> 00:16:43.620
Huh? T-Tatsuya?

00:16:49.880 --> 00:16:50.960
Sorry.

00:16:50.960 --> 00:16:54.300
N-N-No! I-I-I'm fine!

00:16:56.340 --> 00:17:00.810
Is there something you'd like me to do for you
to make up for scaring you like that?

00:17:01.730 --> 00:17:05.730
Something I'd like you to do for me?

00:17:05.730 --> 00:17:08.570
I'm leaving it all to you, Tatsuya.

00:17:08.570 --> 00:17:10.400
Honoka...

00:17:10.400 --> 00:17:13.900
Not like that!
Get away from me, daydream!

00:17:18.620 --> 00:17:20.240
I have all these misgivings.

00:17:20.240 --> 00:17:23.370
I can't believe I'm taking part
in the Nine Schools Competition.

00:17:23.370 --> 00:17:26.830
I'm not as magically skilled as Shizuku,

00:17:26.830 --> 00:17:30.880
and I just know that the players
from the other schools are all incredible.

00:17:30.880 --> 00:17:33.970
I see. In that case...

00:17:33.970 --> 00:17:38.390
we're going to use this spell
at the start of your first Battle Board match.

00:17:38.390 --> 00:17:41.060
What? We're starting with Light Magic?

00:17:41.060 --> 00:17:45.480
No player has succeeded in using Light Magic
to interfere with others until now.

00:17:45.480 --> 00:17:48.480
But I know that you can
pull it off, Honoka.

00:17:48.480 --> 00:17:53.030
This spell was created
from the characteristics of your magic.

00:17:53.030 --> 00:17:56.200
It's your spell and no one else's.
You can be proud of it.

00:17:57.450 --> 00:17:59.620
My spell and no one else's?

00:18:03.910 --> 00:18:06.120
All right! I'm going to be fine!

00:18:06.120 --> 00:18:07.710
On your marks!

00:18:16.630 --> 00:18:17.970
What's this?

00:18:22.430 --> 00:18:23.890
I'm not going to lose.

00:18:23.890 --> 00:18:27.940
This is my spell and no one else's

00:18:27.940 --> 00:18:30.400
because Tatsuya created it for me!

00:18:42.160 --> 00:18:45.870
All right! I did it, Tatsuya!

00:18:47.330 --> 00:18:51.250
That girl sure is using
some interesting moves.

00:18:51.250 --> 00:18:53.840
I can't wait to take her on in the final!

00:18:54.880 --> 00:18:58.590
We will now announce the names of those
taking part in tomorrow's events.

00:18:58.590 --> 00:19:00.430
Shiori...

00:19:00.430 --> 00:19:02.600
Tomorrow's Ice Pillars Break...

00:19:02.600 --> 00:19:03.220
"SHIORI KANOU"

00:19:03.220 --> 00:19:06.140
"SHIORI KANOU"

00:19:03.220 --> 00:19:06.140
I can't let you compete
the way you are now...

00:19:06.140 --> 00:19:11.560
because that would be insulting to your
teammates who've worked so hard until now.

00:19:11.560 --> 00:19:15.570
So, I've decided to replace you.

00:19:15.570 --> 00:19:16.650
I see.

00:19:20.860 --> 00:19:22.660
This is your last chance.

00:19:22.660 --> 00:19:25.490
If you feel up to competing yourself...

00:19:25.490 --> 00:19:29.580
then come to the strategy tent
by 6 AM tomorrow morning.

00:19:29.580 --> 00:19:31.580
No need for that.

00:19:31.580 --> 00:19:34.790
After all, I'm done.

00:19:34.790 --> 00:19:36.670
I'm disappointed in you.

00:19:36.670 --> 00:19:38.300
Just do what you want!

00:19:40.510 --> 00:19:42.680
This is how it should be.

00:19:42.680 --> 00:19:48.480
What Airi was seeking was a talented partner
worthy of the Isshiki Family.

00:19:48.480 --> 00:19:51.730
She has no use for me
and my lack of talent.

00:19:55.190 --> 00:19:57.690
Shiori, do you have a minute?

00:19:59.490 --> 00:20:01.990
Ms. Mizuo, I'm sorry...

00:20:01.990 --> 00:20:03.240
for causing you trouble.

00:20:03.240 --> 00:20:08.290
It's okay. Actually, I wanted
to talk to you about Airi.

00:20:08.290 --> 00:20:12.330
I no longer...

00:20:12.330 --> 00:20:15.540
You've known her since junior high, right?

00:20:15.540 --> 00:20:17.710
At that fencing match.

00:20:17.710 --> 00:20:19.300
I'm so sorry.

00:20:19.300 --> 00:20:23.220
After she discovered me and lifted me up...

00:20:23.220 --> 00:20:26.470
Airi was lifted up just as much as you were.

00:20:28.390 --> 00:20:33.230
See, I've known Airi since we were little
because of our families.

00:20:33.230 --> 00:20:35.310
And thanks to her pride as an Isshiki,

00:20:35.310 --> 00:20:40.740
as well as her talent, which set her apart
from others, she's always been a loner.

00:20:46.700 --> 00:20:50.750
But when she met you...
she was thrilled to have found someone

00:20:50.750 --> 00:20:53.870
she could have a friendly
rivalry with for the first time.

00:20:53.870 --> 00:20:58.460
That was the first time
I'd ever seen Airi looking so happy.

00:20:58.460 --> 00:21:05.840
Competing with a friend... with you, Shiori,
is what made Airi who she is now.

00:21:05.840 --> 00:21:11.890
It's just that Airi can't bring herself to say
just how worried she is about you.

00:21:11.890 --> 00:21:17.900
She could've replaced you sooner, too,
but the reason why she didn't do so...

00:21:17.900 --> 00:21:21.650
You've realized it yourself by now, right?

00:21:21.650 --> 00:21:23.110
If you give up after just one loss...

00:21:23.110 --> 00:21:26.660
you'll never get far as a magician.

00:21:26.660 --> 00:21:30.870
The important thing
is not to let your mind lose.

00:21:30.870 --> 00:21:32.500
Mind...

00:21:32.500 --> 00:21:37.880
As a member of a "One" family, Airi doesn't
give up even if she can't be Number One, right?

00:21:37.880 --> 00:21:41.000
That's why I know
she can become even greater.

00:21:41.000 --> 00:21:42.420
Ms. Mizuo...

00:21:42.420 --> 00:21:43.050
"AUGUST 7, 2095"

00:21:42.420 --> 00:21:43.050
"2095 NATIONAL MAGIC HIGH SCHOOL
GOODWILL TOURNAMENT OF MAGIC SKILLS"

00:21:43.050 --> 00:21:45.760
"AUGUST 7, 2095"
"2095 NATIONAL MAGIC HIGH SCHOOL
GOODWILL TOURNAMENT OF MAGIC SKILLS"

00:21:43.050 --> 00:21:45.760
That's about all that I can say to you.

00:21:45.760 --> 00:21:47.430
"AUGUST 7, 2095"

00:21:45.760 --> 00:21:47.430
"2095 NATIONAL MAGIC HIGH SCHOOL
GOODWILL TOURNAMENT OF MAGIC SKILLS"

00:21:54.140 --> 00:21:56.190
You're late.

00:21:56.190 --> 00:22:00.110
I'm sorry to make you worry.

00:22:00.110 --> 00:22:01.860
I'm all right now.
